A||||4||Back On Holiday||Tail Light bulbs HOT||||5||
Z||000000||Back On Holiday||11-25-2001||08:58 AM||||Q:<BR>Yesterday I was dabbling with some spare taillights for a coupe, had bought a set of red bulbs 1157 I believe, anyway to make this short, I installed 2 lights with red bulbs splitzed into the sockets with the brown/black wire, I cut the reflective section out of section of another tailight <BR>and installed it in that empty space, <BR>that "Empty section" where people do the<BR>PON TIAC glow, except I thought it might be neat to put something else, so I put on<BR>Left  Right<BR>1986  2.8 V6<BR>not very professional, but looks neat.<BR>good prototype if anything else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I chisled the inside of the sockets so I could put in the bulbs backwards so they are Brighter, problem is...after a minute or two, the tailight cover seems very warm.<BR>is there an overheating problem I should worry about?<BR><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-25-2001||09:45 AM||||Brighter bulbs burn hotter.  The brighter look is cool to look at but can melt the plastic from heat build up.  Some where I saw an article about that with just such a warning.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Back On Holiday||12-01-2001||05:23 PM||||I was thinking just the same....maybe i'll put a switch in the dash for them, oh...that gives me an Idea...maybe I could make em say something like "Rice  Sux" for those times when you race a POS ricer and win.  flash those puppys on as they're eating your dust...<P>also...being vulgar, someone else could do one..."EAT  ME"<BR>for those times when you want someone to go road rage on you....J/K<P><P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
